         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/ws250sr1272.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "pencil, five figures run together at the edge of the sheet; read from the lower (180-degree) panel. Figures are plain: a slanted 1, a closed 0 with no descender, a second 1, a 2 with a horizontal base, and a double-bowled 3. Month and year are not in doubt, January 1923. The day is: 10123 could be read 10.1.23 or 1.01.23, and I take the first because this workshop writes a single-figure month unpadded, as in 14114 for 14.1.1914."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
